The getBlob endpoint won't return any uploaded blobs until they've been successfully "anchored" to at least one post record.

If we beautify your JSON, the issue becomes apparent - you haven't put the embed field inside the `record` object, and therefore it's being ignored silently. Since it never gets properly attached to the post, getBlob pretends it doesn't exist.

```json
{
  "embed": {
    "images": [
      {
        "image": {
          "ref": {
            "$link": "bafkreigeo6ukmjkdnw2iujtuwonrohcnb35wngjzkprzh5ojowzosmkhoq"
          },
          "size": 311430,
          "$type": "blob",
          "mimeType": "image/jpg"
        },
        "alt": "brief alt text description of the image"
      }
    ],
    "$type": "app.bsky.embed.images"
  },
  "repo": "did:plc:vo37i5ooqwooxgkmbc3277kt",
  "record": {
    "text": "Image API Test posted at {ts '2023-11-09 15:47:45'}",
    "createdAt": "2023-11-09T15:47:45-07:00",
    "langs": [
      "en-US"
    ],
    "type": "app.bsky.feed.post"
  },
  "collection": "app.bsky.feed.post"
}
```

For anyone having similar issues.

I had to create a /.well-known/did.json 

Ensure FEEDGEN_SERVICE_DID is commented out so that app.bsky.feed.describeFeedGenerator shows the did:web:hostingdomain.org

did.json was in the format:

```
{
  "@context": [
    "https://www.w3.org/ns/did/v1"
  ],
  "id": "did:web:hostingdomain.org",
  "service": [
    {
      "id": "#bsky_fg",
      "type": "BskyFeedGenerator",
      "serviceEndpoint": "https://hostingdomain.org"
    }
  ]
}
```

I filtered these out in my implementation using something like this:

```

  onError: (err) => {
    if (
      err instanceof FirehoseParseError &&
      err.event.ops?.some((a) => a.action === "delete")
    ) {
      return;
    }
    console.error(err);
  },
```

I use flutter, this is what I did:

```
Future<void> postAvatar(File file) async {
  final session = await _session;
  var bsky = await getBsky(session);
  final image = file.readAsBytesSync();
  final response = await bsky.atproto.repo.uploadBlob(bytes: image);
  bsky.actor.profile.put(avatar: response.data.blob);
}
```
